<%# ── MODAL 3: $2.3T OCO ── %>
<dialog id="oco-modal" class="hm-dialog" aria-labelledby="hm-oco-title">
  <div class="hm-header">
    <button class="hm-close" onclick="this.closest('dialog').close()" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
    <div class="hm-eyebrow">◆ Islamic Jihad Cost Database · Overseas wars</div>
    <div class="hm-headline" id="hm-oco-title">$2.3T</div>
    <p class="hm-subtitle">The cost of Afghanistan, Iraq, and Syria — before veteran care</p>
  </div>
  <div class="hm-body">
    <div class="hm-stats">
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">~$825B</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">Afghanistan (2001–2021)</div></div>
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">~$1.1T</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">Iraq (2003–present)</div></div>
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">2,461</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">U.S. military deaths, Afghanistan</div></div>
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">20 yrs</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">Length of Afghan war</div></div>
    </div>
    <ul class="hm-facts">
      <li>OCO (Overseas Contingency Operations) funding was always processed as emergency supplementals — never in the base defense budget — making it invisible to routine budget oversight for two decades.</li>
      <li>At peak (2011): 100,000 U.S. troops in Afghanistan plus 45,000 in Iraq simultaneously — two major ground wars at once, both funded off-budget.</li>
      <li>America's longest war ended August 30, 2021 — 20 years, 4 months after it began. The Taliban returned to Kabul within days of withdrawal.</li>
      <li>The Iraq War alone cost more in real dollars than the Marshall Plan — the program that rebuilt all of Western Europe after World War II.</li>
      <li>Neither war was formally declared by Congress under Article I. Both operated under the 2001 Authorization for Use of Military Force, which has never been repealed.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="hm-srcs">
      <div class="hm-srcs-lbl">Sources</div>
      <p class="hm-srcs-list">
        <a href="https://watson.brown.edu/costsofwar/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Brown University, Costs of War Project (2021)</a>
        &middot;
        <a href="https://www.sigar.mil/allreports/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SIGAR — Special Inspector General for Afghanistan</a>
        &middot;
