<%# ── MODAL 5: 15% DISCRETIONARY ── %>
<dialog id="discretionary-modal" class="hm-dialog" aria-labelledby="hm-disc-title">
  <div class="hm-header">
    <button class="hm-close" onclick="this.closest('dialog').close()" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
    <div class="hm-eyebrow">◆ Islamic Jihad Cost Database · Budget share</div>
    <div class="hm-headline" id="hm-disc-title">15%</div>
    <p class="hm-subtitle">One in seven discretionary dollars, every year for fifteen years</p>
  </div>
  <div class="hm-body">
    <div class="hm-stats">
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">2002–17</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">Period of Stimson Center analysis</div></div>
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">~4%</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">Pre-9/11 CT share of discretionary</div></div>
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">~$68B</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">Avg annual Education Dept budget</div></div>
      <div class="hm-stat"><div class="hm-stat-val">26</div><div class="hm-stat-lbl">Budget documents Stimson had to compile</div></div>
    </div>
    <ul class="hm-facts">
      <li>The Stimson Center found no federal agency tracked the counter-terrorism total — they had to compile it from 26 separate budget documents published by different departments over 15 years.</li>
      <li>CT's share of discretionary jumped from ~4% pre-9/11 to 15% — a near-quadrupling — and has never returned to the pre-9/11 level despite the end of major combat operations.</li>
      <li>The entire Department of Education averages ~$68B/year — CT spending absorbed 1.5 to 2× that amount annually in the 2002–2017 period.</li>
      <li>Transportation and infrastructure averaged ~$90B/year in the same window — less than two-thirds of the counter-terrorism share of the budget.</li>
      <li>If CT spending had remained at its pre-9/11 share (4% of discretionary), cumulative 2002–2017 savings would have exceeded $2 trillion.</li>
    </ul>
    <div class="hm-srcs">
      <div class="hm-srcs-lbl">Sources</div>
      <p class="hm-srcs-list">
        <a href="https://www.stimson.org/2018/counterterrorism-spending-protecting-america-while-promoting-efficiencies-and-accountability/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stimson Center, Counterterrorism Spending (2018)</a>
        &middot;
        <a href="https://www.whitehouse.gov/omb/budget/historical-tables/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Office of Management and Budget — historical tables</a>
        &middot;
        <a href="https://www.cbo.gov/topics/defense-and-national-security" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Congressional Budget Office</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="hm-share-bar">
      <span class="hm-share-lbl">Share</span>
      <button class="hm-share-btn hm-share-x"         data-share="x"><i class="ti ti-brand-x"></i> X</button>
      <button class="hm-share-btn hm-share-linkedin"   data-share="linkedin"><i class="ti ti-brand-linkedin"></i> LinkedIn</button>
